 "_named_about": "M3-CHR-540: `named` holds the named Stillguards, each built like a variant (build_stillguard.py --variant <id>) but output under its own id (assets/characters/<id>/, the dialogue's speaker id) and never one of the six squad variants. A named entry carries the same keys as a variant plus `_seed` (its skin and hair noise seed, where a variant uses ord(<letter>)) and in `_variant` `spear` (false: no spear, the right hand free) and `broken_tooth` (the chip off the upper central incisor, its depth as a share of the crown's height). M4-A2P-051: `_variant` may also take `halberd` (true: sg_halberd's halberd on the spear's bone), `shield` (false: no shield) and `palette` (the costume's dyes, sg_textures.dyed_cloth), and the entry its own `_costume` keys over the squad's.",
